{
  "case_id": "2020-20-472",
  "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (HollyFrontier Cheyenne Refining LLC)",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute establishing the Renewable Fuel Standard exempted all small refineries from its requirements for the first years of the program and authorizes them individually to seek extensions of that exemption at any time based on hardship."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (HollyFrontier Cheyenne Refining LLC)",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Nothing in the statute's text imposes this unique prohibition. Respondents' argument rests on the word \"extension,\" which they contend should be read temporally here to mean an increase in a length of time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chief Justice Roberts: So this really is a -- a freestanding exemption, and --in your view, and I wonder -- I'm not saying it's an inconceivable construction, but is this the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chief Justice Roberts: Counsel, I -- I -- I think you would agree that there's no Chevron deference issue here because the agency has changed its position, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: One last question.\nOn your alternative reading, the one that you\nsuggested to the Chief Justice, if we were to\naccept that \"extension\" is not -- doesn't\nrequire continuity, wouldn't that result in the --\nand I think you acknowledge that small\nrefineries that came into the scene after 2006\ncould never receive an exemption, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Let me shift gears and see if there's another provision in the statute that might help you. Section 7545(o)(7)(A) allows the EPA to waive the RFP requirements upon a finding that they would severely harm the economy of a state or region. I could imagine a small refinery, you know, if it -- if it were struggling or if it were going to be forced out of business, that that might harm the economy of a region. Is that a provision that might help you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federal Respondent",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MICHEL: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Under the key provision in this case, a small refinery may seek an extension of the exemption under subparagraph (A). The meaning of that language is straightforward. If a small refinery has an exemption under subparagraph (A), it can obtain an extension of that exemption from EPA. But, if a small refinery no longer has the exemption, it cannot obtain an extension. EPA cannot grant something that does not exist. That is the ordinary, common-sense meaning of the statutory text."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: In your definitions that you provide for \"extend\" in your -- in your brief, they seem to assume words like \"continuance\" or \"continuation,\" which seem to suggest that at some point there was a --a termination or an interruption and then a resumption. Do you have any that preclude continuity -- that -- that assume continuity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, I'd like to go back to something you said to Justice Alito. You said that this is not going to close -- not going to cause small refineries to close. Please explain why."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "EPA denied about 18 petitions between 2013 and 2015, and as far as we know, only one small refinery went out of business after that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Good morning, Mr. Michel. I'd -- I'd like to address with you the point I -- I discussed with Mr. Keisler about Footnote 6 in his reply brief and whether there's a continuity requirement in (A) which might shed some light on whether we think there's a continuity requirement in (B). Is he correct that it would be"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Why wouldn't that -- why wouldn't that have been possible, given that we'd be looking at different years in '04 and '06?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: No, I understand -- I understand, factually, it didn't happen, but, conceptually, could it have happened?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0003-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: How about 10 days later?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0003-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Good morning, Mr. Michel. I want to make sure I have a handle on what you mean by \"ambiguous.\" You said a couple times that the word \"extension\" is ambiguous, and -- and I would have thought that by that, you mean that it does have several definitions which we've gone over during argument and in the briefs, if you look in a dictionary, but that in the context of this statute, it's clear which of those definitions -- or reasonably clear that there's a better indication of which of those definitions is the right one. Am I understanding your argument correctly?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0003-0013",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Well, I mean, not necessarily unambiguously correct, because, you know, we're here arguing back and forth about what it might mean. But I don't think you mean to say that we could not glean which way in which Congress was using the word \"extension\" when we look at the context, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what's your interest in Petitioner not receiving this extension?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that you're -- you are not selling enough ethanol? Is that what I'm hearing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0004-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So it's part of your argument that in context, there's a continuity requirement to the word \"exemption,\" but so long as they are continuous, can these exemptions go on into perpetuity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0004-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there's nothing in the text that stops a small refinery from continually getting the exemption year after year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-472",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f46442e9a45dafac9f735c531e5f003c9ea7f28e02b84ee8af86daabe74559d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f46442e9a45d-0004-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 97,
        "start": 97
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "doesn't really mean temporary, then maybe it doesn't cast as much light as you say on what \"exemption\" means either."
    },
    {
